  "id": "Compound::DB06589 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Pazopanib is linked to Cyp2c8 through a series of indirect but plausible mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Pazopanib may act as a substrate for Cyp2c8, as it is included in the category of Cytochrome P450 2c8 inhibitors, which includes Trimethoprim. This implies that Pazopanib could potentially inhibit Cyp2c8 activity, though the direct interaction remains unclear. Additionally, Pazopanib is associated with Skin Depigmentation and Anal Haemorrhage, both of which are linked to Cyp2c8 through the binding of Mometasone and Apixaban, respectively. These findings suggest that Pazopanib may influence Cyp2c8 through multiple pathways, possibly by affecting the metabolic clearance of other compounds that bind to the enzyme. The integration of these mechanisms highlights the potential for Pazopanib to modulate Cyp2c8 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
